          "partner": "analyst",
          "position": "Exactly. The unit economics look extraordinary right now, but they're based on one assumption I can't verify: churn. At 2% monthly churn my LTV/CAC math shows 11x. At 5% monthly churn — which is not unusual for SMB SaaS targeting owner-operators — it collapses to about 4x. Still above the floor, but a very different story. I'd also want to know if the $1,200 CAC is fully loaded or just direct spend. Founders often exclude their own selling time from that number."
        },
